# ===================================================================================#
# GWIscan family table — FAMILY mode (one flat list of families)                     #
# ===================================================================================#
# Copy this file to  config/family.tsv  and edit it for your study families,
# and set  MODE: family  in config.yaml.
#
# One row per family. TAB-separated. Whole-line '#' comments and blank lines are
# ignored (put each comment on its own line beginning with '#').
#
# COLUMNS
#   Family        Study family name. Used verbatim in outputs and in systematic
#                 domain ids (e.g. GNA -> AthGNA001.1). Required and unique.
#
#   PfamModel     How the family is IDENTIFIED — one of three forms, told apart
#                 automatically:
#                   PFxxxxx   a Pfam accession. The HMM is downloaded from InterPro
#                             and searched with hmmsearch; DIAMOND also runs.
#                   name.hmm  a custom, family-specific HMM you built and placed in
#                             db/hmm/ (its NAME line must equal the Family). Searched
#                             with hmmsearch; DIAMOND also runs. Use this when the
#                             family's Pfam is a shared/ancestral domain not specific
#                             to the family.
#                   -         no HMM. Identified by DIAMOND alone.
#
#   BlastModel    Reference protein FASTA (in db/blast/) used as the DIAMOND round-1
#                 query. DIAMOND runs for every family, so this is required for all.
#
#   InterProModel Optional. Accession(s) that CONFIRM a candidate via InterProScan.
#                 A candidate is kept when it carries any of them, so a family with no
#                 usable Pfam still confirms on another database. One of three, by
#                 prefix: PF... (Pfam), cd... (CDD), PTHR... (PANTHER). Pipe-separated
#                 for alternatives (PF01476|PTHR27007 confirms on either). GWIscan
#                 enables the matching InterProScan applications automatically. Leave
#                 blank to confirm on
#                 the PfamModel accession; a family with neither is not gated.
#
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
Family	PfamModel	BlastModel	InterProModel
# specific Pfam -> hmmsearch + DIAMOND, confirmed on that Pfam (InterProModel blank):
GNA	PF01453	AAA33346.1.fasta
Legume	PF00139	AAA33983.1.fasta
# no usable Pfam -> DIAMOND, confirmed on a CDD accession:
CRA	-	ABL98074.1.fasta	cd02879
# no usable Pfam -> DIAMOND, confirmed on a PANTHER accession:
EUL	-	ABW73993.1.fasta	PTHR31257
